def battery-sense (v_out = 2.75 V, i = 275 uA)
  title "Battery voltage measurement: divider switched by a P-MOSFET, hold capacitor at the ADC"
  about "A 1:2 divider (10 kΩ + 10 kΩ) reads the battery at an ADC pin, but only while a GPIO asks for it: Q2
      (AO3400A) pulls the gate of the high-side Q1 (AO3401A) low, Q1 connects the divider to the battery; otherwise R1
      holds Q1 off and the divider draws nothing – a permanent 100 k + 100 k divider would draw 21 µA from a 4.2 V
      cell all the time. 100 nF at the ADC pin, as Espressif asks for at ADC inputs, hold the voltage while the
      converter samples. Switching the divider's low side instead would pull the ADC pin up to the full battery
      voltage while off."
  port bat "the voltage to measure: the cell's plus (lipo-charger's cell) or another supply up to 5.5 V"
  port en "the GPIO that switches the measurement on (high = measure)"
  port adc "to the ADC pin: half the battery voltage while en is high, 0 V otherwise"
  port gnd "ground"
  part Q1 transistor AO3401A lcsc C15127 "{as}: divider switch, high side"
    notes "Source at bat, drain at the divider. Off, its body diode would conduct only from the divider back to bat –
      the divider never rises above bat."
  part R1 resistor 0805W8F1003T5E lcsc C149504 value 100k "{as}: Q1 gate to bat 100 k"
    notes "Holds Q1 off. While measuring it draws bat / 100 kΩ (42 µA at 4.2 V)."
  part Q2 transistor AO3400A lcsc C20917 "{as}: level shift for Q1"
    notes "A 3.3 V GPIO cannot switch Q1 off directly: on a 4.2 V cell its gate would sit at −0.9 V, inside the
      AO3401A's threshold range (−0.5 … −1.3 V). Q2 pulls the gate to ground instead."
  part R2 resistor 0805W8F1003T5E lcsc C149504 value 100k "{as}: en pull-down 100 k"
    notes "Keeps Q2 and with it the divider off while the GPIO floats (reset, deep sleep without hold); 33 µA from the
      GPIO while measuring."
  part R3 resistor 0805W8F1002T5E lcsc C17414 value 10k "{as}: divider top 10 k"
  part R4 resistor 0805W8F1002T5E lcsc C17414 value 10k "{as}: divider bottom 10 k"
  part C1 capacitor CC0805KRX7R9BB104 lcsc C49678 value 100nF "{as}: hold capacitor 100 nF at the ADC"
    notes "Espressif's schematic checklist: a 0.1 µF filter capacitor between an ADC pin and ground. With the
      divider's 5 kΩ: τ = 0.5 ms – read about 5 ms (10 τ) after en goes high."
  net bat Q1.source R1.1
  net gate @bat Q1.gate R1.2 Q2.drain
  net top @bat Q1.drain R3.1
    notes "Top of the divider: bat while measuring, 0 V otherwise."
  net adc 0..2.75 V R3.2 R4.1 C1.1 fn adc
    notes "Half of bat: 2.1 V for a full Li-ion cell (4.2 V), 2.75 V for 5.5 V."
  net en Q2.gate R2.1
  net gnd Q2.source R2.2 R4.2 C1.2
  derive R3.value R4.value divider(v_out, i, in = bat)
  covers REQ.value/adc LIM.range/adc REQ.function LIM.range/gate LVL.undefined
  notes "Divider 1:2 (R3 = R4 = 10 kΩ, ±1 %): a Li-ion cell of 3.0–4.2 V gives 1.5–2.1 V, inside the ESP32's window at
      11/12 dB attenuation (150–2450 mV, ESP-IDF v4.4 ADC documentation) and the 3.3 V of an RP2040/RP2350. Above 4.9
      V on bat the ESP32 window is left (LIM.range/adc warns where the MCU's entry gives adc.range_v); for 2S packs or
      12 V another ratio – keep the adc net's v in step."
  notes "Source resistance at the ADC pin: R3 ∥ R4 = 5 kΩ – within the 10 kΩ the Arduino Nano's entry (A000005,
      ATmega328P) allows even without the hold capacitor (REQ.value/adc). A larger divider (100 k + 100 k: 50 kΩ)
      draws less while measuring but needs the hold capacitor and ten times the settling time; switched, the current
      hardly matters."
  notes "The adc net carries fn adc: REQ.function wants an ADC-capable pin on it, LIM.range/adc holds it to the pin's
      window. On the ESP32 take an ADC1 pin: ADC2 is shared with Wi-Fi, its reads block while Wi-Fi runs (ESP-IDF v4.4
      ADC documentation)."
  notes "Reading: en high, wait about 5 ms (C1 through 5 kΩ, τ 0.5 ms), read, en low. Per reading about 0.2 mA through
      the divider and 42 µA through R1 for those milliseconds; off, nothing flows but the leakage of Q1 and Q2."
  notes "bat above 5 V: Q2 pulls Q1's gate to ground while measuring, so |VGS| = bat – the AO3401A allows ±12 V,
      edakit's derating 67 % of it (8 V). Above that a zener from gate to source, and in any case another divider
      ratio with the adc net's v in step."
  notes "sim.json: the en net under the MCU's outputs and a load that sets it high (gpio) – the scenario shows the
      voltage at the ADC; in the others en is low and the divider dark."
  set test {
     "connect": {
      "bat": "+5V",
      "en": "SIG",
      "adc": "VBAT_ADC"
     },
     "nets": {
      "VBAT_ADC": [
       0,
       2.75
      ]
     },
     "sim": {
      "mcu": {
       "U1": {
        "outputs": [
         "LED_SDI",
         "LED_CLK",
         "LED_LE",
         "LED_OE",
         "SIG"
        ],
        "pullups": [
         "BTN"
        ],
        "pullup_ohm": 50000
       }
      },
      "loads": {
       "measure": {
        "about": "firmware reads the battery: SIG high, LEDs off",
        "gpio": {
         "LED_OE": 1,
         "SIG": 1
        },
        "leds_on": []
       }
      }
     }
     }
